        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): bound cursor pagination with MAX_PAGES=50",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`collectSlackCursorPages` uses an unbounded `do..while(cursor)` loop. Adding an explicit safety bound prevents infinite pagination in pathological cases, while throwing a clear error when exhausted makes truncation visible to callers.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/slack/src/cursor-pages.ts`:\n  - Replace `do..while(cursor)` with `for (page 0..49) { ... if (!cursor) return }` bounded loop\n  - Export `SLACK_CURSOR_PAGES_MAX = 50`\n  - Add exported `SlackCursorPagesExhaustedError` thrown when the 50-page budget is exceeded and a `next_cursor` still exists\n- `extensions/slack/src/cursor-pages.test.ts`: 6 tests covering normal completion, multi-page collection, exhaustion error, error detail check, empty page, null cursor\n\n## Review Response\n\nPer ClawSweeper review (P1): \"Fail when the page budget is exhausted — throw an explicit exhaustion error or return typed truncation instead of discarding it.\"\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests (all pass)\n\n```\n  ✓ collects items from a single page when no cursor is returned\n  ✓ collects items across multiple pages while cursor is present\n  ✓ throws SlackCursorPagesExhaustedError when cursor remains at MAX_PAGES limit\n  ✓ includes the page count in the exhaustion error\n  ✓ handles empty response from collectPageItems\n  ✓ handles null/undefined next_cursor\n```\n\n### Real behavior proof — local exhaustion test\n\n```\n=== Case 1: Normal completion (cursor ends after 3 pages) ===\n  ✓ collected 3 pages, 3 fetchPage calls\n\n=== Case 2: Single page (no cursor returned) ===\n  ✓ collected 1 items\n\n=== Case 3: Exhaustion (cursor never ends, hits 50 page limit) ===\n  ✓ Slack cursor pagination exhausted after 50 pages; response still contains a next_cursor, data may be incomplete\n  ✓ pageCount=50\n```\n\n### Lint + type check + caller tests\n\n```\nnpx tsc --noEmit: no errors\nresolve-channels.test.ts: 4 passed\nresolve-users.test.ts:    3 passed\n```\n\n## Diff\n\n```diff\n-const SLACK_CURSOR_PAGES_MAX = 50;\n+export const SLACK_CURSOR_PAGES_MAX = 50;\n\n+export class SlackCursorPagesExhaustedError extends Error {\n+  override readonly name = \"SlackCursorPagesExhaustedError\";\n+  readonly pageCount: number;\n+  constructor(pageCount: number) { ... }\n+}\n\n export async function collectSlackCursorPages<TItem, TResponse>(...):\n   for (let page = 0; page < SLACK_CURSOR_PAGES_MAX; page += 1) {\n     ...\n     if (!cursor) {\n-      break;\n+      return items;\n     }\n   }\n+  throw new SlackCursorPagesExhaustedError(SLACK_CURSOR_PAGES_MAX);\n }\n```\n",
